From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mkiring <haohao.wang@seeed.cc>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rockusb: allow Loader entry on empty eMMC (no GPT)

cmd/rockusb.c already special-cases nvme/scsi devnum 0 by appending
":0" so rkusb_init() tolerates a missing partition table. mmc was
left out, so an empty eMMC blocks Loader entry and sends the board
into a reboot loop ("Enter rockusb failed, fallback to bootrom...").

Extend the same fallback to mmc 0.

Signed-off-by: Mkiring <haohao.wang@seeed.cc>
---
 cmd/rockusb.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmd/rockusb.c b/cmd/rockusb.c
--- a/cmd/rockusb.c
+++ b/cmd/rockusb.c
@@ -231,7 +231,8 @@
 	if (!strcmp(devtype, "mmc") && !strcmp(devnum, "1")) {
 		pr_err("Forbid to flash mmc 1(sdcard)\n");
 		return CMD_RET_FAILURE;
-	} else if ((!strcmp(devtype, "nvme") || !strcmp(devtype, "scsi")) && !strcmp(devnum, "0")) {
+	} else if ((!strcmp(devtype, "nvme") || !strcmp(devtype, "scsi") ||
+		    !strcmp(devtype, "mmc")) && !strcmp(devnum, "0")) {
 		/*
 		 * Add partnum ":0" to active 'allow_whole_dev' partition
 		 * search mechanism on multi storage, where there maybe not
